# The folder is a named build context (`hive_data`) of the images that install
# it, and a named context reads the .dockerignore in its own folder, not the
# one at the root of hive-mind (which keeps modules/ out of the mind image).
# pip needs pyproject.toml, README.md and hive_data/ and nothing else.
**/__pycache__
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info
build/
dist/
.pytest_cache/
.venv/
tests/
docs/
.git
